# Table & Pagination Patterns

## Table Implementation
```tsx
<Table
  isLoading={isLoading}
  data={transformedData}
>
  {({ Column }) => (
    <>
      <Column name="name" label="Name" />
      <Column 
        name="status" 
        label="Status" 
        render={(row) => (
          <Badge intent={MAP_STATUS_BADGE_INTENT[row.status]}>
            {row.status}
          </Badge>
        )}
      />
      <Column 
        name="amount" 
        label="Amount" 
        render={(row) => formatCurrency(row.amount)}
      />
      <Column 
        name="id" 
        label="Actions"
        render={(row) => (
          <Button size="sm" onClick={() => handleEdit(row)}>
            Edit
          </Button>
        )}
      />
    </>
  )}
</Table>
```

## Pagination Pattern
```tsx
const [filter, setFilter] = useState({});

<Pagination
  data={data?.meta}
  onChange={(page) => setFilter(prev => ({ ...prev, page }))}
/>
```

## Badge Mapping Pattern
```ts
const MAP_STATUS_BADGE_INTENT = {
  ACTIVE: "success",
  INACTIVE: "default",
  PENDING: "warning",
  FAILED: "danger",
} as const;
```

## Best Practices
- Provide `data` already transformed for display
- Use `isLoading` prop for loading states
- Custom cell UI through `render` function
- Keep `Pagination` directly below `Table`
- Always enable `keepPreviousData` in queries for smooth transitions
- Status/enum columns should map to `Badge` components
- Currency formatting via `formatCurrency()` utility
- Action buttons in dedicated `Column name="id"`

## Query Integration
```ts
const { data, isLoading } = useEntityListQuery(filter);
```

